<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caucasus campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1914">1914</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> campaign was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> in which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and other states, in the Caucasus and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> from 1914 to 1918. After the Ottoman disaster at Sarikamish (1914–1915), Russia advanced as far as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzurum">Erzurum</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trabzon</a>; after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-revolution">Russian Revolution</a> the Ottomans counter-attacked into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-caucasus">Transcaucasia</a>, where Armenian forces checked them at Sardarabad in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caucasus-campaign.jpg" alt="Caucasus campaign" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caucasus_campaign.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
